{"name":"Oliva Oscuro","hex":"#665439","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oliva","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["olivary body"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oliva"},{"term":"oscuro","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cigar made with very dark tobacco."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oscuro"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oliva","blocks":[{"text":"Oliva is a municipality in the comarca of Safor in the Valencian Community, Spain. To its east lie 10 kilometres of coastline and beaches fronting the Mediterranean Sea, and 8 kilometres to the north is Gandia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Ajuntament_d%27Oliva%2C_la_Safor.JPG/330px-Ajuntament_d%27Oliva%2C_la_Safor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oliva","wikidata":"Q918586"},{"title":"Cigar","blocks":[{"text":"A cigar is a rolled bundle of dried and fermented tobacco leaves made to be smoked. Cigars are produced in a variety of sizes and shapes. Since the 20th century, almost all cigars are made of three distinct components: the filler, the binder leaf which holds the filler together, and a wrapper leaf, which is often the highest quality leaf used. Often there will be a cigar band printed with the cigar manufacturer's logo. Modern cigars can come with two or more bands, especially Cuban cigars, showing Limited Edition bands displaying the year of production."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Cigar_tube_and_cutter.jpg/330px-Cigar_tube_and_cutter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cigar","wikidata":"Q1576"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Mediterranean_Sea_in_Oliva%2C_Valencia_Region_of_the_Spain_02.JPG/500px-Mediterranean_Sea_in_Oliva%2C_Valencia_Region_of_the_Spain_02.JPG?utm